# No Dev Server or IDE Browser

Do not start local dev servers or open the IDE browser unless the user explicitly asks.

## Do not

- Run `npm run dev`, `pnpm dev`, `quasar dev`, or similar to "verify" UI changes
- Start background dev servers "for browser verification"
- Use the IDE browser MCP (`browser_navigate`, `browser_snapshot`, `browser_tabs`, etc.) to preview the app
- Open `http://localhost:*` in the IDE browser after making changes

## Do instead

- Rely on typecheck, lint, or tests when the user asked for verification
- Tell the user to open the app in their own browser if visual confirmation is needed
- Only start a server or use the IDE browser when the user clearly requests it (e.g. "start dev server", "open in browser", "check the dashboard in browser")
